IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cr1-interpretation`
IMPORT `cr1-helpers`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), PART II -- INFORMATION RETURNS (regulations 9 to 14).
-- Piece cr1. LAYER 1: the law as the text states it.
--
-- A return is "filed with the Minister" (the Minister of National Revenue in Part II: regulation 2(1)(a)). The
-- form is "prescribed" (fork F8 in NOTES.md). A "last day of February" is worked out from the year, so a leap
-- year gives the 29th.

§ `Regulations, Part II -- information returns (regs 9 to 14)`

§§ `Regulation 9: interpretation`

-- 9 In this Part, all words and expressions have the same meaning as in Part I. The rule says only which Part's
-- words Part II uses; it is silent for any other Part (NOTHING).
-- src:197 | 9 In this Part, all words and expressions have the same meaning as in Part I.
@ref Reg 9 (src:197)
GIVEN part IS A `cr1 Part of the Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE `cr1 Part of the Regulations`
`reg 9 — the Part whose words and expressions a Part uses` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `the Regulations' Part II` THEN JUST `the Regulations' Part I`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 10: filing of employer's returns`

-- 10 (1) Subject to subsection (2), every person who has made a payment of remuneration during a year to an
-- employee employed by him in pensionable employment shall, without notice or demand, file with the Minister
-- an information return for that year in prescribed form on or before the last day of February of the year
-- next following.
-- src:200 | 10 (1) Subject to subsection (2), every person who has made a payment of remuneration during a year to an employee employed by him in pensionable employment shall, without notice or demand therefor, file with the Minister an information return for that year in prescribed form on or before the last day of February of the year next following.
@ref Reg 10(1) (src:200)
GIVEN `the person has made a payment of remuneration during the year to an employee employed by the person in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 10(1) — the person must file an information return for the year` `the person has made a payment of remuneration during the year to an employee employed by the person in pensionable employment` MEANS
    `the person has made a payment of remuneration during the year to an employee employed by the person in pensionable employment`

@ref Reg 10(1) (src:200)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 10(1) — the last day of February of the year next following` year MEANS
    (YearMonthDay (year PLUS 1) 3 1) PLUS (0 MINUS 1)

-- 10 (2) A person carrying on a business or activity with respect to which they employ employees in
-- pensionable employment shall, if they cease to carry it on, within 30 days of so ceasing and without notice
-- or demand, file with the Minister, with respect to those employees, the information return required by
-- subsection (1). Subsection (1) is "subject to" (2): as in regulation 8(2), the day is the earlier of the two
-- (fork F7).
-- src:201 | (2) A person carrying on a business or activity with respect to which he employs employees in pensionable employment shall, if he ceases to carry on that business or activity, within 30 days of so ceasing and without notice or demand therefor, file with the Minister, with respect to those employees, the information return required by subsection (1).
@ref Reg 10(2) (src:201)
GIVEN `the day the person ceased to carry on the business or activity` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 10(2) — the day by which an information return must be filed after ceasing to carry on a business` `the day the person ceased to carry on the business or activity` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the day the person ceased to carry on the business or activity` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 30)

@ref Reg 10(1), 10(2) (src:200), (src:201)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day the person ceased to carry on the business or activity` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 10 — the day by which the information return for a year must be filed` year `the day the person ceased to carry on the business or activity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the person ceased to carry on the business or activity`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `reg 10(1) — the last day of February of the year next following` year
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN
        `cr1 helper: the earlier of two dates`
            (`reg 10(1) — the last day of February of the year next following` year)
            (`reg 10(2) — the day by which an information return must be filed after ceasing to carry on a business` ceased)

-- 11 Every person who makes or has made a payment of remuneration at any time to an employee employed in
-- pensionable employment shall, on demand by registered letter from the Minister, make an information return in
-- prescribed form containing the information required and file it with the Minister within such reasonable time
-- as may be stipulated in the registered letter. The "reasonable time" is the Minister's judgment: the day the
-- letter stipulates is an input and the rule is conditional on it being reasonable.
-- src:202 | 11 Every person who makes or has made a payment of remuneration at any time to an employee employed in pensionable employment shall on demand by registered letter from the Minister make an information return in prescribed form containing the information required therein and shall file the return with the Minister within such reasonable time as may be stipulated in the registered letter.
@ref Reg 11 (src:202)
GIVEN `the person makes or has made a payment of remuneration at any time to an employee employed in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has demanded the return by registered letter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11 — the person must make an information return on demand` `the person makes or has made a payment of remuneration at any time to an employee employed in pensionable employment` `the Minister has demanded the return by registered letter` MEANS
    `the person makes or has made a payment of remuneration at any time to an employee employed in pensionable employment` AND `the Minister has demanded the return by registered letter`

@ref Reg 11 (src:202)
GIVEN `the day the return was filed` IS A DATE
      `the day stipulated in the registered letter, if the Minister is satisfied that it is a reasonable time` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11 — the return demanded was filed in time` `the day the return was filed` `the day stipulated in the registered letter, if the Minister is satisfied that it is a reasonable time` MEANS
    `the day the return was filed` AT MOST `the day stipulated in the registered letter, if the Minister is satisfied that it is a reasonable time`

§§ `Regulation 12: legal representatives and others`

-- 12 (1) When a person who is required to make a return under this Part for a year dies before having made it,
-- the return shall be filed by the person's legal representatives within 90 days of the death and shall be in
-- respect of that year or, if the return is required in respect of the year in which the person dies, in
-- respect of that part of it before the death.
-- src:205 | 12 (1) When a person who is required to make a return under this Part for a year dies before having made the return, the return shall be filed by his legal representatives within 90 days of his death and shall be in respect of that year or, if the return is required in respect of the year in which he dies, in respect of that part thereof prior to his death.
@ref Reg 12(1) (src:205)
GIVEN `the day the person died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 12(1) — the day by which the legal representatives must file the return` `the day the person died` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the day the person died` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)

@ref Reg 12(1) (src:205)
GIVEN `the year the return is required for` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the person died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 12(1) — the last day the return covers` `the year the return is required for` `the day the person died` MEANS
    IF (DATE_YEAR `the day the person died`) EQUALS `the year the return is required for`
    THEN `the day the person died`
    ELSE YearMonthDay `the year the return is required for` 12 31

-- 12 (2) Every trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, trustee or committee and every
-- agent or other person administering, managing, winding up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the
-- property, business or estate of a person who has not filed a return for a year as required by this Part shall
-- file the return on that person's behalf.
-- src:206 | (2) Every trustee in bankruptcy, assignee, liquidator, curator, receiver, trustee or committee and every agent or other person administering, managing, winding-up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the property, business or estate of a person who has not filed a return for a year as required by this Part shall file such return on that person’s behalf.
@ref Reg 12(2) (src:206)
DECLARE `cr1 Capacity in which a person deals with another's property, business or estate` IS ONE OF
    `a trustee in bankruptcy`
    `an assignee`
    `a liquidator`
    `a curator`
    `a receiver`
    `a trustee`
    `a committee`
    `an agent or other person administering, managing, winding up, controlling or otherwise dealing with the property, business or estate`
    `none of those`

@ref Reg 12(2) (src:206)
GIVEN capacity IS A `cr1 Capacity in which a person deals with another's property, business or estate`
      `the other person has not filed a return for the year as required by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 12(2) — the person must file the return on the other's behalf` capacity `the other person has not filed a return for the year as required by this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER capacity
    WHEN `none of those` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `the other person has not filed a return for the year as required by this Part`

§§ `Regulation 13: distribution of the employee's portion of the return`

-- 13 (1) Every person required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for a year with the Minister
-- shall supply to each employee in respect of whose remuneration the return relates two copies of the portion of
-- the return relating to that employee.
-- src:209 | 13 (1) Every person required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for a year with the Minister shall supply, to each employee in respect of whose remuneration the return relates, two copies of the portion of the return relating to that employee.
@ref Reg 13(1) (src:209)
GIVEN `the person is required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 13(1) — the number of copies of the employee's portion the person must supply` `the person is required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for the year` MEANS
    IF `the person is required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for the year`
    THEN JUST 2
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 13 (2) The copies shall, on or before the day the return is required to be filed with the Minister, be sent
-- to the employee by mail at the employee's latest known address or be delivered to the employee in person.
-- src:210 | (2) The copies referred to in subsection (1) shall, on or before the day the information return is required to be filed with the Minister, be sent to the employee by mail at his latest known address or be delivered to him in person.
@ref Reg 13(2) (src:210)
GIVEN `sent by mail at the employee's latest known address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `delivered to the employee in person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the copies were sent or delivered` IS A DATE
      `the day the return is required to be filed with the Minister` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 13(2) — the copies were supplied in the way and by the day required` `sent by mail at the employee's latest known address` `delivered to the employee in person` `the day the copies were sent or delivered` `the day the return is required to be filed with the Minister` MEANS
        (`sent by mail at the employee's latest known address` OR `delivered to the employee in person`)
    AND `the day the copies were sent or delivered` AT MOST `the day the return is required to be filed with the Minister`

-- 13 (3) A person may send an information return, as required under (1), in an electronic format if the person
-- has received the employee's express consent in writing or in an electronic format; in that case the person
-- shall send a single copy to the employee on or before the day the return is to be filed with the Minister.
-- 13 (4) A person who has not received that consent may still provide the information return to the employee in
-- an electronic format unless the person is precluded from doing so under subsection 209(5) of the Income Tax
-- Regulations (not deposited, so an input); the person shall send a single copy on or before the day the return
-- is to be filed.
-- src:211 | (3) A person may send an information return, as required under subsection (1), in an electronic format if the person has received the express consent of the employee in writing or in an electronic format and, in that case, the person shall send a single copy of the information return to the employee on or before the date on which the return is to be filed with the Minister.
-- src:212 | (4) A person who has not received the express consent of the employee in accordance with subsection (3) may still provide the information return to the employee, as required under subsection (1), in an electronic format unless the person is precluded from doing so under subsection 209(5) of the Income Tax Regulations. The person shall send a single copy of the information return to the employee, on or before the date on which the return is to be filed with the Minister.
@ref Reg 13(3), 13(4) (src:211-212)
GIVEN `the person has received the employee's express consent in writing or in an electronic format` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is precluded from providing it electronically under subsection 209(5) of the Income Tax Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 13(3) and (4) — the person may supply the employee's portion in an electronic format` `the person has received the employee's express consent in writing or in an electronic format` `the person is precluded from providing it electronically under subsection 209(5) of the Income Tax Regulations` MEANS
        `the person has received the employee's express consent in writing or in an electronic format`
    OR  (NOT `the person is precluded from providing it electronically under subsection 209(5) of the Income Tax Regulations`)

@ref Reg 13(1), 13(3), 13(4) (src:209), (src:211-212)
GIVEN `the person is required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person supplies the employee's portion in an electronic format` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person may supply it in an electronic format` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 13 — the number of copies the employee must be given` `the person is required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for the year` `the person supplies the employee's portion in an electronic format` `the person may supply it in an electronic format` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is required by section 10 or 12 to file an information return for the year`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person supplies the employee's portion in an electronic format` AND `the person may supply it in an electronic format`
         THEN JUST 1
         ELSE JUST 2

§§ `Regulation 14: penalties`

-- 14 (1) Every person who fails to file a return as and when required by this Part is liable to a penalty of
-- $10 for each day of default, but not exceeding in all $250. (2) Every person who fails to comply with
-- section 13 is liable to the same penalty. The amount is stated once.
-- src:215 | 14 (1) Every person who fails to file a return as and when required by this Part is liable to a penalty of $10 for each day of default, but not exceeding in all $250.
-- src:216 | (2) Every person who fails to comply with section 13 is liable to a penalty of $10 for each day of default, but not exceeding in all $250.
@ref Reg 14(1), 14(2) (src:215-216)
GIVEN `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 14 — the amount of the penalty for a number of days of default` `the number of days of default` MEANS
    min 250 (10 TIMES (max 0 `the number of days of default`))

-- The days of default are the days from the day the act was due until the day it was done.
-- src:215 | 14 (1) Every person who fails to file a return as and when required by this Part is liable to a penalty of $10 for each day of default, but not exceeding in all $250.
@ref Reg 14(1) (src:215)
GIVEN `the day by which the act was due` IS A DATE
      `the day the act was done` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 14 — the number of days of default` `the day by which the act was due` `the day the act was done` MEANS
    max 0 ((Day `the day the act was done`) MINUS (Day `the day by which the act was due`))

@ref Reg 14(1) (src:215)
GIVEN `the person fails to file a return as and when required by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 14(1) — the penalty for failing to file a return as and when required` `the person fails to file a return as and when required by this Part` `the number of days of default` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to file a return as and when required by this Part`
    THEN JUST (`reg 14 — the amount of the penalty for a number of days of default` `the number of days of default`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:216 | (2) Every person who fails to comply with section 13 is liable to a penalty of $10 for each day of default, but not exceeding in all $250.
@ref Reg 14(2) (src:216)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with section 13` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 14(2) — the penalty for failing to comply with section 13` `the person fails to comply with section 13` `the number of days of default` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with section 13`
    THEN JUST (`reg 14 — the amount of the penalty for a number of days of default` `the number of days of default`)
    ELSE NOTHING
